{"availability":"available","full":"peternewnham/react-html-parser","name":"react-html-parser","description":"Converts HTML strings directly into React components and provide a simple way to modify and replace the content.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":797,"forks":102,"created":"2016-01-18T23:58:36Z","updated":"2024-06-28T08:15:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://peternewnham.github.io/react-html-parser","topics":["html","react"],"demo":"https://wrakky.github.io/react-html-parser","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.532Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.532Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.532Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.532Z","stars":797,"forks":102}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A utility for converting HTML strings into React components. Converts standard HTML elements, attributes and inline styles into their React equivalents and provides a simple way to modify and replace the content.","Including a sanitizer as part of the library means it is making decisions for you that may not be correct. It is up to you to decide what level of sanitization you need and to act accordingly. Some users may already be sanitizing on the server or others may have specialized requirements that cannot be covered by a generic implementation.","Additionally, HTML sanitization is a hard thing to get right and even the most popular and actively developed sanitizers have vulnerabilities discovered from time to time. By leaving the sanitization outside of this library it gives users the ability to patch and deploy any fixes needed immediately instead of having to wait for a new version of this library to be released with the fix."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/peternewnham/react-html-parser/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"54c35a08a8900ead485798da4bf32763176908090033cc441c552bc08d038ae3","extractedAt":"2026-10-05